WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.190
If it isn't Onodera!

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.190
Mr. Sumi!

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.490
Right now I'm editing shojo manga.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.700
Shojo manga?

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.610
But why?

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.690
I read you as a man of literature,
through and through.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.390
Yes,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.790
I guess you could say
a lot has happened.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.620
Mr. Takano.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.090
Sir...

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.440
This is my boss. He's
Emerald's editor-in-chief.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.090
Masamune Takano.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.380
Shojo manga are nice,

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.350
but Onodera here is really
more suited to literature.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.600
Don't keep him here too long.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.600
Oh, yeah. Are you interested in
reading Mr. Sumi's latest book?

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:54.490
<i>I guess I always did like literature.</i>

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.400
<i>Did that come out of Takano's room?</i>

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:01.700
Hey!

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.310
You stay inside.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.230
This guy he had gone out with in
high school suddenly kicked him out,

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:17.880
and disappeared without giving him
a chance to find out the reason.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.780
Years pass,

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.890
and just when I thought
he was finally over it,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:28.680
some old classmate of that guy
found a clue or something.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:35.650
Apparently that guy had a fiancé at
the time he was dating Masamune.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.180
So the one guy who asked him
out was dating two people.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.660
How many people around Masamune
do you think fit that profile?

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.920
No, it wasn't like that!

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:52.630
That thing with the fiancé
was a misunderstanding!

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.900
Misunderstanding or not,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.560
nothing will change the fact
that you hurt Masamune!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:28.540
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:28.540
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:34.090
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:34.090
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.720
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.720
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:44.510
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:44.510
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:49.520
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:49.520
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.360
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.360
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.740
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.740
If I reach out my hand

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.110
hajimete no kimochi

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.110
Will you understand my feelings?

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.490
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.490
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.870
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.870
I love you more and more every second

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:15.000
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:15.000
We're still far from a happy ending

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:23.970
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:23.970
But I want to make it come true

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.430
tsuzuite yuku

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.430
Our story continues

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.490
I finally managed to get him to recover.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.580
Don't come strolling in
and try to steal him away!

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.370
Yokozawa?

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.000
What are you doing here?

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.200
Remember my email about
dropping this guy off?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.240
Oh, yeah.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.480
The food is in the usual place.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:00.740
Yeah.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:06.110
Hey, did you get fat?

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.510
He didn't. It's just his winter coat.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.270
Sorata, is that true?

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.020
Hey, Onodera, you...

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:22.620
E-Excuse me! Good night!

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.280
Hey!

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:28.230
Masamune, come inside quickly.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.430
Sorata.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.330
<i>I remember now, that cat...</i>

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.570
<i>It's the cat he took
in a long time ago.</i>

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.920
<i>It was raining and everybody ignored</i>

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:46.530
<i>the meowing, abandoned
cat except for him.</i>

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.240
Sorata...

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.230
<i>Why is Yokozawa taking care of him?</i>

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.350
<i>I hurt Takano...</i>

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.170
<i>Takano knew me longer than I thought...</i>

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.120
<i>Those are all random misunderstandings.</i>

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.390
<i>I'm sick of it!</i>

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.330
<i>Everything's always so confusing...</i>

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.270
<i>...when Takano gets involved.</i>

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.990
<i>I wonder what's going on.</i>

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.470
<i>Whenever Takano's near,
something feels off.</i>

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:37.100
<i>I can clearly tell that I lose
my calm when he's around.</i>

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.040
<i>This affair is long over.</i>

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.550
<i>It might have been fine when I
was nothing but a naive student,</i>

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.470
<i>but right now I'm a working adult.</i>

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.490
<i>My relationship to Takano
is that he's my boss.</i>

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.250
<i>And we're both guys.</i>

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:05.380
<i>Besides, people always say
that your first love...</i>

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.990
<i>...never works out.</i>

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:13.990
<i>That's why I need to make a clean
break and focus only on work.</i>

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:18.870
<i>But if I stay around him like this,</i>

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:20.740
<i>I will...</i>

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.780
<i>Marukawa's pretty flexible
when it comes to transfers.</i>

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:38.290
<i>Maybe I should submit a transfer
request for the literary department.</i>

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.250
<i>I mean that's the reason
I quit my old job.</i>

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.200
<i>And to be honest, I think I'm
more suited for literature.</i>

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.090
<i>In the past I was always
in charge of star authors,</i>

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.890
<i>but we did do better
than other companies.</i>

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.270
<i>I wonder how it would go now.</i>

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.690
Oh, yeah, I got an email.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.440
<i>It might be impossible to produce
results in just three months,</i>

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.860
<i>even then, I'm always
making small mistakes</i>

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.880
<i>and Takano's always yelling at me.</i>

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.990
<i>The workload and exhaustion
levels are at an all time high.</i>

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:18.410
<i>This room's really messy,
even for a guy's room.</i>

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.590
<i>When was the last time
I slept on my bed?</i>

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:32.220
<i>Why am I editing manga again?</i>

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.470
You dropped these papers when you fell.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:40.850
Be more careful!

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.770
Oh, thank you.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.360
Please just drop them in the mailbox.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.610
Huh? What the hell is wrong with you?!

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:55.110
Uh, thank you very much.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.480
See you.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.830
What do you want?!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.570
I wanted to ask something.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:01.490
What?

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.580
Do you really want to go to
the literature department?

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.260
Uh, that's...

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.920
Oh, I'm sorry. I think
it's from the company.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:17.350
Go ahead.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.040
Sure.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:26.750
My apologies, but I had forgotten
to get in touch with you.
The manuscripts have been returned
from the printer so
we sent them to Mutou's house.
Please tell her right away.
Thank you very much.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.720
It's from manufacturing.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:26.770
Apparently they're returning the
manuscript for Mutou's next book.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.130
Call her to tell her about it.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.280
Yeah, sure, but...

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.220
I'll just wait here.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.840
<i>Can't he just go home?</i>

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.580
<i>Mutou speaking.</i>

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.100
Good evening, this is Onodera
from Marukawa publishing.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:53.010
<i>Oh, good evening!</i>

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.190
I wanted you to know
that we've returned

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:58.350
your manuscript for the next book

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.030
<i>Ah, thank you.</i>

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:02.810
I think it'll arrive some time tomorrow,

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.940
so please be aware of that.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:09.880
<i>This was the one where the
flu outbreak happened, right?</i>

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.800
That was quite a rough ride, huh?

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.450
<i>You even helped me with the
screentone at the airport.</i>

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.690
Actually, when I got
home and took a bath,

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.560
I was shocked because some
screentone floated up.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.220
<i>Really? To be honest,</i>

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:28.510
<i>I don't quite remember
what happened after that.</i>

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:32.970
Well, let's just say

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.600
that everything is okay,
considering the book got done.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.620
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.890
<i>Oh, Onodera?</i>

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:39.660
Yes?

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.550
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:44.390
For what?

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.770
<i>Now I can actually tell you this,</i>

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:51.560
<i>but when I heard this was your
first time editing manga,</i>

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:55.000
<i>I thought that it was
the worst thing ever.</i>

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:55.990
<i>But in reality,</i>

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.990
<i>you worked really hard and
put a lot of love into the book.</i>

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:03.490
<i>Your advice for the storyboard
and plot was accurate as well.</i>

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:06.160
<i>For an author, the editor is...</i>

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.650
<i>...the first place the work goes
before it's released to the world,</i>

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:16.240
<i>so I'm glad that you became my editor.</i>

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.640
<i>Hello? Onodera? Hello?</i>

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.520
Uh, thank you!

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:31.080
Let's sell this book!

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.580
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:36.330
Ah, yes! Please give it your best, too!

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:37.430
Goodbye.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.030
What should I do?

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.030
She praised me.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.280
<i>It's probably just a
standard compliment,</i>

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:56.110
<i>something to encourage the
new editor even though</i>

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:57.520
<i>he's not doing anything special.</i>

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:02.050
<i>Since I didn't know what to do,</i>

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:05.880
<i>I was always struggling just to
follow Takano's instruction</i>s.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.230
<i>I bet the people around me </i>

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.440
<i>feel a little anxious when
they see me like that.</i>

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:19.520
<i>Actually, I really do worry if
what I'm doing is good enough.</i>

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:22.200
<i>But...</i>

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.410
<i>But since I'm so simple,</i>

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.620
<i>if something small I did is </i>

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:33.040
<i>recognized and praised, even a little,</i>

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.210
<i>all the hard times are
forgotten in an instant.</i>

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.090
Takano.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:46.100
And I can't help but be happy.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.850
Do you think I can become
a proper manga editor?

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.360
Where did that come from?

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:59.010
I was just thinking
about things and I...

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.610
Did she say something to you?

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:03.920
Not really.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.220
<i>He's sharp.</i>

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:10.680
Well, she just encouraged
me a little on the phone.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.120
What did she say?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.050
Well,

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.560
something like she was
glad I was her editor.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:24.840
I know, it's probably just
a standard compliment.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:29.460
I think it's the worst to have
an author worry about you.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.720
Why?

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:39.400
Isn't that the ultimate
praise for an editor?

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:43.900
Just so you know,

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.910
I never thought that you
couldn't be a manga editor.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.660
If I had thought that,

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.300
I would have never let
you do the work you did.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.860
You finally looked at me properly.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:07.030
If you don't have an answer
now, that's fine, too.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:07.910
See you.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.650
Takano!

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:17.500
Thank you very much!

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:22.170
Blood.

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:23.240
Huh?

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:25.670
There's blood there.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.850
Is that from when you fell before?

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.100
Lame.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:35.810
Huh? But my pants aren't torn.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:37.920
It's probably a friction burn.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:40.880
Do you have disinfectant?

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.650
No.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:43.960
Seriously?

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.690
Come with me, I have some.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.210
No, it's fine.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:48.560
I'll just rinse it off with water.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:49.720
You idiot, it'll get infected!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.280
No, it's really fine!

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:53.720
Why?

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:55.830
Because...

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.470
At your place...

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:58.730
Yokozawa is...

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:12.940
No, it's fine.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:14.260
I'll just rinse it off with water.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.410
You idiot, it'll get infected!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.950
No, it's really fine!

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:19.420
Why?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.460
Because...

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.180
At your place...

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.420
Yokozawa is...

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.480
He left ages ago.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.690
He has a business trip to Kyushu
first thing in the morning.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.660
Wait here.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.520
<i>That was awkward...</i>

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.930
<i>I have to lock the door.</i>

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:11.250
<i>Then we're just going back to
being boss and subordinate.</i>

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:17.680
<i>I have to do it quickly...</i>

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.750
What am I doing?

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.110
Sorry, I'm out of big band-aids.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:35.490
I only have a bandage.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.320
Oh, it's already fine.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:40.110
I'll do the rest myself.

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:41.750
Don't worry about it.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.750
It's half my fault that you fell.

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:49.440
I don't think that's true.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:59.770
Did Yokozawa say something to you?

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:04.270
Not really.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:08.780
We've known each other since college.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:14.280
I started working at Marukawa
because he recommended it.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:17.690
He's always been like that,

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.990
but he's really just a very caring guy.

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:24.360
He always studied hard and worked hard.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:30.300
So you can always ask him
about work related things.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:33.060
He's a very good salesman,

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:34.610
so if you ask him proper questions,

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:36.700
he should always give you advice.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.180
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.740
<i>I'm thinking about something
totally unrelated.</i>

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:48.930
<i>Were you and Yokozawa going out?</i>

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:55.260
<i>Why does he have a key to your place?</i>

00:16:56.390 --> 00:17:01.800
<i>Is it true that you got
hurt because of me?</i>

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.330
<i>There are just too many
things I want to ask.</i>

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:08.820
Onodera?

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:13.800
<i>But what would asking
these things achieve?</i>

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:18.850
What's wrong?

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:21.850
<i>What is...</i>

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:24.850
Onodera...

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:29.360
<i>...the answer I want?</i>

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:31.610
Sto-

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:35.200
Don't run, Ritsu!

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.310
<i>No.</i>

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:50.200
<i>No.</i>

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.350
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.590
<i>I'm going to...</i>

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:02.140
<i>...get sucked in.</i>

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.390
Onodera, I want you.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.900
<i>Oh, no...</i>

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:12.460
<i>What do I do...
I need to say no...</i>

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.870
<i>I have to push him away,</i>

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:21.620
<i>but my head is all mushy inside...</i>

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.910
Onodera, I love you.

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:30.830
<i>I don't want this...</i>

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.310
<i>Because it's Takano...</i>

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:36.390
<i>I want...</i>

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.830
Who the hell?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:47.060
I'm sorry, it's Mutou.

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:48.690
Answer it!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.490
S-Sure.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:52.630
Onodera speaking.

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:55.460
Yes, it's fine.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.510
About the corrections
for the storyboard?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:02.700
Yes, just one second, I'll go get them.

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:06.010
No, it's really fine!

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:13.190
<i>Seriously, wake up. What
the hell am I doing?</i>

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:16.110
<i>I totally succumbed
to the flow just now!</i>

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:18.910
Sorry for the wait.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:21.340
Go ahead and tell me where
you have questions.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:24.420
Yes, I have plenty of time!

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:29.350
That frame is... One second.

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:29.330
Please hurry up and leave.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:52.180
<i>Hello? Hello, Onodera?</i>

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.620
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:19:55.740 --> 00:20:00.680
Yes, I think I'm okay...

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.230
<i>I knew it,</i>

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:09.020
<i>I hate Takano.</i>

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:22.120
I've finished the material
for the next meeting,

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.040
the development plan
for next month's issue,

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:26.870
as well as some other things.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.160
What's up? You're so enthusiastic.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:36.260
I just thought I'd try to work
with a different mindset.

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.420
But you were doing fine until now, too.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.780
Well, I think that besides work,

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.430
you need to keep your
personal life in order.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.240
I'm trying to become a
proper manga editor...

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:50.150
...on the foundation of properly
cooking three meals for myself

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:51.430
and keeping my house clean.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:56.520
Oh, yeah, I remember having
those useless thoughts.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.610
Yep.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.440
Why are you looking at me with pity?!

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.390
Are you stupid?

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:04.990
If you have time for nonsense like that,

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:07.200
get your next task done.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.450
Takano!

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:10.950
What?

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.380
If I seriously master
being a manga editor,

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:16.960
you'll be out of your job!

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.330
You heard that, Mr. Isaka?

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:25.300
Wow, really? I'm looking
forward to that.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.930
I uh...

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:31.400
Good luck, Takano. You're
really in danger.

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:33.260
Yes, what should I do about that?

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:41.060
This isn't a joke.
I'm going to quit this job!

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:44.630
This isn't love! This isn't
love! This isn't love!

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:48.750
I will never admit that this is love!

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:58.710
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:58.710
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:04.090
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:04.090
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:12.180
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:12.180
I fell in love with you

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:15.690
yuugure no kaze no nioi

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:15.690
In a sunset, filled with the scent of the wind

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:20.610
boku wa omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:20.610
When I remember your voice and your smile

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:25.530
kimi no koe sono waraikata

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:25.530
I'm instantly happy

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:29.820
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:29.820
I fell in love with you

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:33.750
dare ni mo mada ietenai

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:33.750
But I haven't been able to tell anyone yet

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:38.210
hitori omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:38.210
When I remember your voice and the way you talk

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:42.710
sono koe shaberi kata

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:42.710
Even though I'm alone I'll be happy

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:47.880
samishii kimochi potsuri

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:47.880
The feeling of loneliness... isolated

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:51.300
sukina kimochi kirari

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:51.300
The feeling of love... sparkling

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:56.810
futatsu kubetsu ga tsukanai boku wa

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:56.810
I'm unable to tell these two feelings apart

00:22:56.850 --> 00:23:01.440
yuugure ni kokoro tsuburete ku

00:22:56.850 --> 00:23:01.440
My heart is slowly crushed as the sun sets

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.820
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.820
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:10.280
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:23:05.990 --> 00:23:10.280
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:14.660
asa no hikari ga afure dashitara

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:14.660
Once the morning light pours in

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:20.750
suki to yuou yuuki motte

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:20.750
I'll courageously say I love you
